// Myrnohrad, part II, The road (Дорога): 3 December 2025, the short day. The corridor is about a kilometre wide
// (c15 §3), nothing on wheels gets through by day, and their drones own the road (c15 §5). The plan wanted a clear
// day of 3-7 December; ERA5 has none (design/myrnohrad.md, progress): the 3rd is the least grey of the week, dry and
// calm under 95% cloud, 4 °C, the ground bare. No fog, so their drones fly at the day's full tempo from first light
// to dusk; their infantry seeps in at the clear day's rate; what comes in comes by ground robot and, at dusk, by the
// Vampire (c15 §5), and the wounded wait for the robots. The day starts from part I's aftermath as the Record has it:
// the cars burnt on the road, the south-eastern edge's post gone, wounded still waiting at the mine and the high-rise.
// The schema is bav_core::data and bav_sim::data; the map is map.ron.
(
    date: "3 December 2025",
    tally_date: "03 DEC 2025",
    // 08:00 to sunset, 15:40, in the day's 1500 s.
    day_start_min: 480.0,
    compression: 0.307,
    // No snow yet that week (ERA5: snow depth 0 from 1 to 15 December): the late autumn's bare, frozen ground.
    season: Autumn,
    // 3 December is the 337th day of the year; Kyiv on UTC+2.
    sun: (337, 2.0),
    // Under cloud all day, dry, a light easterly (ERA5: 95% cloud, 9 km/h from the east).
    overcast: true,
    wind: (-2.0, 0.0, -1.55),
    // Half the town's roofs gone by now, more ruins smouldering, the cars of three weeks on the road.
    ruined: (0.5, 11),
    smouldering: 16,
    cars: [
        ((-1445.8, -213.4), 1.28),
        ((-2102.3, -382.4), 1.61),
        ((-517.5, -89.7), 2.04),
        ((721.8, -313.2), -1.4),
        ((-1577.9, -236.6), -1.4),
        ((428.1, -297.3), -1.31),
        ((-614.5, -94.7), -1.76),
        ((332.8, -285.0), -1.69),
        ((-1217.2, -152.5), -1.6),
        ((-1674.8, -263.9), 1.66),
        ((-750.0, -75.8), -1.46),
        ((-1721.7, -285.3), -1.35),
        ((-815.8, -94.3), 1.72),
        ((-449.5, -98.9), 1.12),
        ((168.1, -270.1), 2.22),
        ((-2084.5, -377.9), -1.38),
    ],
    words: (
        briefing: r#"MYRNOHRAD (МИРНОГРАД), THE ROAD INTO THE POCKET
3 DECEMBER 2025, DAY

Two days ago Moscow announced that Pokrovsk had fallen. A NATO official says Myrnohrad is virtually encircled. The
corridor out to the north is a kilometre wide, and the one road in, through Rivne and Svitle, is watched from the
air every hour of the day. Nothing on wheels gets through it in daylight; what comes in comes by robot, by heavy
bomber drone, or on foot at night. The wounded wait: three of them have waited since yesterday or longer.

You are the same drone team, in the same basement. The garrison still holds Svitle, Rivne, the western quarters
and the mine. Today there is no fog. Their FPV crews fly all day, their Orlans come over the road, and their
infantry still comes in by twos and threes, fewer on a day like this, and goes for the drone crews first. You have
six ground robots, the Vampire for the dusk, three interceptors, two EW domes, and nets over the road from the
edge to the town.

Your task today: get the wounded onto the robots, so that no more than six are still waiting at dusk, and keep
Svitle and the western quarters.

Mouse: right-drag to look, wheel to zoom.  WASD: fly the drone.  Q/E: turn.  R/F: climb/descend.  I: thermal.
Left click: 155 mm fire mission (4 rounds).  4: an FPV.  C: drop a grenade from the drone.
V: a ground robot for the wounded.  Alt+click: a robot with ammunition.  7: the robot's camera.  8: the Vampire.
9: an interceptor.  J: our EW domes off and on (they blind our own FPVs too).
1/2 or Tab: drone / the observers on the high-rise.  M: move the drone team when they find you.  P: pause.  [ ]: time.

Press Enter."#,
        op_label: "OBSERVERS, A NINE-STOREY ROOF ON SOBORNA STREET (СПОСТЕРІГАЧІ, ДЕВ'ЯТИПОВЕРХІВКА НА СОБОРНІЙ)",
        op_lost: "The observers on the high-rise are gone. No eyes from the roof.",
        forward_belt: "the ruins",
        mine_lines: ["Mine. He's stopped.", "Another one on a mine.", "Mine on the verge. That one's done."],
        closing: [
            "On 8 December the 7th Corps pulled out of the salient south of Pokrovsk. On the 10th the exits from Myrnohrad were reported to be collapsing.",
            "On 27 December Russia claimed Myrnohrad. ISW saw them in about half of it.",
        ],
        keys: "R: the same day again, on the same road.     Esc: quit.",
        sources: [
            (
                publisher: "Euromaidan Press",
                date: "27 Nov 2025",
                title: "Russia doesn't need to storm Myrnohrad—just wait for a sunny day",
                url: "https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/11/27/road-into-myrnohrad/",
            ),
            (
                publisher: "European Pravda",
                date: "2 Dec 2025",
                title: "NATO says Myrnohrad is \"virtually encircled\" and Russians control over 95% of Pokrovsk",
                url: "https://www.eurointegration.com.ua/eng/news/2025/12/2/7226211/",
            ),
            (
                publisher: "Euromaidan Press",
                date: "10 Dec 2025",
                title: "\"Impossible to stop them, they're everywhere\": Ukraine holds Pokrovsk against 170,000 Russians, but Myrnohrad evacuation routes collapse",
                url: "https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/12/10/impossible-to-stop-them-theyre-everywhere-ukraine-holds-13-sq-km-of-pokrovsk-against-170000-russians-but-myrnohrad-evacuation-routes-collapse-video/",
            ),
            (
                publisher: "Institute for the Study of War",
                date: "28 Dec 2025",
                title: "Russian Offensive Campaign Assessment, December 28, 2025",
                url: "https://understandingwar.org/research/russia-ukraine/russian-offensive-campaign-assessment-december-28-2025/",
            ),
        ],
    ),
    // The day's task (bav_core::data::Goal): the wounded brought out against the queue at dusk, three of them waiting
    // since yesterday or longer at first light (c15 §5: days, by November up to two weeks); and Svitle and the western
    // quarters ours, the road in through Svitle with them (c15 §2, 14 Nov; §3). A wounded man aboard a robot is no
    // longer waiting. The Record, as history had it, leaves the queue longer at dusk than at dawn: 7, 8, 8 and 10
    // waiting in seeds 0-3, so the goal asks a little more than the record did; Svitle and the western quarters ours
    // in three (in the fourth the western quarters contested).
    objective: [
        (
            name: ("The wounded waiting at dusk", "Поранені в черзі до сутінків"),
            test: WoundedWaiting(6),
            met: "The robots kept the queue of the wounded short. In December most robots did not survive the trip, and every one that came back with men aboard was a day or a week less of waiting.",
            missed: "The queue of the wounded was longer at dusk than the day could carry, as it was that winter: men waited days for a robot, some two weeks, and a robot marked with a red cross drew fire.",
        ),
        (
            name: ("Svitle and the western quarters", "Світле і західні квартали"),
            test: Held(["svitle", "west"]),
            met: "Svitle and the western quarters were ours at dusk, and the road in through Svitle with them. Russia would claim the town on 27 December; it was still being fought for in January.",
            missed: "Svitle or the western quarters were theirs at dusk. Historically both held through December, and the road through Svitle was the last way into the pocket.",
        ),
    ],
    // The debrief's rows (the schema is the game's screen.rs); the tally's and the fire panel's lines are map.ron's.
    debrief: (
        rows: [
            Line("Their men sent in", Sent),
            Line("    dead", AttackerDead),
            Line("    came back", Returned),
            Line("Our casualties", DefenderLosses),
            Areas("{area} at the end"),
            Line("Shells left", Shells),
            If(Drops, [Line("Grenades dropped from the drone", Drops)]),
            If(
                Robots,
                [
                    Line("Ground robots", Robots),
                    Line("    loads delivered", Delivered),
                    Line("Wounded brought out by robot", WoundedCarried),
                    Line("    still waiting", WoundedWaiting),
                ],
            ),
            If(Bomber, [Line("The Vampire's sorties", Sorties)]),
            If(Killzone, [Line("Their FPVs over the road", TheirSorties), Line("    what they hit", TheirHits)]),
            If(
                Seep,
                [
                    Line("Their burrows in the town", Burrows),
                    Line("    found", BurrowsFound),
                    Line("    emptied", BurrowsEmptied),
                    Line("Their fire on our drone crew told", CrewsHit),
                ],
            ),
        ],
    ),
    op: ((868.0, 495.0), 30.0),

    // The pocket on 3 December: the corridor about 1 km wide north of the box (c15 §3); theirs closer on the
    // south-western fields, the south-eastern edge theirs (c15 §2, 14 Nov), the jaw over the north-eastern corner.
    // The road in stays ours to Rivne.
    pocket: (
        grey: [
            [
                (-5000.0, -400.0),
                (-2400.0, -380.0),
                (-1500.0, -50.0),
                (-300.0, 450.0),
                (700.0, 600.0),
                (1600.0, 750.0),
                (5000.0, 600.0),
                (5000.0, 5000.0),
                (-5000.0, 5000.0),
            ],
            [(500.0, -5000.0), (5000.0, -5000.0), (5000.0, -150.0), (1700.0, -350.0), (900.0, -1000.0)],
        ],
        theirs: [
            [
                (-5000.0, -250.0),
                (-2400.0, -200.0),
                (-1600.0, 300.0),
                (-400.0, 800.0),
                (700.0, 950.0),
                (1500.0, 1100.0),
                (5000.0, 1000.0),
                (5000.0, 5000.0),
                (-5000.0, 5000.0),
            ],
            [(1000.0, -5000.0), (5000.0, -5000.0), (5000.0, -500.0), (1800.0, -700.0), (1200.0, -1300.0)],
        ],
    ),
    // The garrison's posts: Svitle, Rivne, the western quarters, the high-rise, the mine, the western entrance; and
    // the road head's EW mast, where the robots leave the H-32, with no riflemen.
    ua_positions: [
        (-560.0, -1250.0),
        (-1750.0, -700.0),
        (-100.0, 250.0),
        (500.0, 400.0),
        (880.0, 525.0),
        (1400.0, -300.0),
        (300.0, -150.0),
        (-2150.0, -470.0),
    ],
    // Theirs on the south-eastern edge since mid-November (c15 §2, 14 Nov: the flag on a ruined mine there): a
    // position in the ruins by mine No. 3's heap; its strength is the design's.
    ru_positions: [(1250.0, 1450.0)],

    // ---- The battle's part (bav_sim::data) ----
    // Ground robots and a heavy bomber (c15 §5: every supply run into the town by drone or UGV, and the UGVs "usually
    // don't survive the trip"; bombers lift 60 mm bombs, never 120 mm). Six robots and two sorties of the Vampire for
    // the dusk (the allotment's, below): five of the robots the Record's runs, and one for a call that has waited two
    // hours of the clock (`fetch`). The wounded wait for a robot, and three already wait at first light from the days
    // before (c15 §5: days, by November up to two weeks): two at the mine and one at the high-rise; the numbers and
    // the hours are the design's. With their drone crews on the road the per-kilometre stand-in is off.
    // What each post has to fire before it is dry, as in the fog (fog.ron, the design's): a robot's load of
    // ammunition or the Vampire's bundle fills it by half.
    post_ammo: 60,
    // Their position on the south-eastern edge: riflemen only.
    ru_weapons: [None],
    robots: (
        casevac: true,
        waiting: [(post: 5, n: 2, hours: 30.0), (post: 4, n: 1, hours: 14.0)],
        fetch: 2.0,
        bomber: (endurance: 900.0),
    ),
    // The Record: riflemen at the seven posts, a battery's sixteen rounds, eight FPVs, eight grenades for the drone.
    allotment: (
        points: 80,
        supply: (6, 1.0),
        record: [
            (id: "rifles", at: 0),
            (id: "rifles", at: 1),
            (id: "rifles", at: 2),
            (id: "rifles", at: 3),
            (id: "rifles", at: 4),
            (id: "rifles", at: 5),
            (id: "rifles", at: 6),
            (id: "155", count: 1),
            (id: "fpv", count: 8),
            (id: "vog", count: 4),
            (id: "robot", count: 6),
            (id: "vampire", count: 2),
        ],
    ),
    // Their drones over the road (bav_sim::killzone; c15 §4, §5): the same crews as in the fog, at the full day's tempo
    // from first light on a dry day, Rubikon on the road all day (it held the single road "almost constantly under
    // fire control", c15 §5). Our two EW domes: over the drone team at the town's western entrance, and at the road
    // head, where the robots leave the H-32 for the villages' tracks; nets over the road's west stretch, from the
    // edge past Rivne and Svitle to the town's western entrance, and over the robots' track from the road head down
    // to Rivne as far as the road's watchers see (the stretch is the design's). No car on the road in the Record:
    // nothing on wheels gets through by day (c15 §5). The rates are the design's (c15 §11).
    killzone: (
        crews: [
            (name: ("Rubikon", "Рубікон"), kind: Fibre, at: (600.0, 2900.0), per_hour: 14.0, budget: 12),
            (
                name: ("Sudny Den", "Судний день"),
                kind: Rf,
                at: (-900.0, 2600.0),
                per_hour: 10.0,
                relay: (-700.0, 1620.0),
            ),
            (
                name: ("the Irish", "«Ірландці»"),
                kind: Rf,
                at: (2800.0, -2300.0),
                per_hour: 8.0,
                relay: (2250.0, -1650.0),
            ),
            (name: ("the Archangels", "«Архангели»"), kind: Fibre, at: (2700.0, 2200.0), per_hour: 6.0),
            (name: ("the Archangels", "«Архангели»"), kind: Waiter, at: (-1240.0, -162.0), per_hour: 2.0),
            (name: ("the Archangels", "«Архангели»"), kind: Waiter, at: (-560.0, -86.0), per_hour: 2.0),
            (name: ("the Archangels", "«Архангели»"), kind: Waiter, at: (-1100.0, 392.0), per_hour: 2.0),
        ],
        // The H-32 from the road head into the town, and the northern road by Rivne's north.
        watch: [
            [
                (-2304.0, -448.5),
                (-1795.4, -302.3),
                (-1573.0, -240.2),
                (-1240.7, -150.3),
                (-779.5, -83.9),
                (-415.7, -105.0),
                (-199.3, -202.5),
                (14.4, -247.8),
                (628.6, -368.4),
                (1076.7, -414.0),
            ],
            [(-2304.0, 35.6), (-1218.6, 367.3), (-1003.4, 384.6), (-833.1, 332.8), (-674.8, 212.8), (-437.9, -80.9)],
        ],
        domes: [(post: 6, radius: 300.0), (post: 7, radius: 300.0)],
        nets: [
            [
                (-2304.0, -448.5),
                (-1795.4, -302.3),
                (-1573.0, -240.2),
                (-1240.7, -150.3),
                (-779.5, -83.9),
                (-718.8, -82.4),
                (-415.7, -105.0),
            ],
            [
                (-2128.0, -398.0),
                (-2111.0, -393.0),
                (-2100.0, -415.0),
                (-2061.0, -504.0),
                (-2013.0, -607.0),
                (-1911.0, -567.0),
                (-1845.0, -593.0),
                (-1787.0, -633.0),
                (-1761.0, -676.0),
            ],
        ],
        // Their direction-finders locate our drone team's ground station about once an hour of drone time.
        team: 1.0,
    ),
    // Their reconnaissance wings and our interceptors (bav_sim::wings; 01 e7, e9): on a dry day their Orlans and ZALAs
    // come over the road through the day, four passes against the drone team's three interceptors and the radar that
    // cues them. The times and paths are the design's.
    wings: (
        passes: [
            (
                at: 230.0,
                kind: Orlan,
                path: [(-200.0, 5200.0), (-700.0, 300.0), (-1700.0, -500.0), (-1300.0, 5200.0)],
            ),
            (
                at: 700.0,
                kind: Zala,
                path: [(2900.0, -3200.0), (1200.0, -600.0), (-200.0, -300.0), (2500.0, -3600.0)],
                agl: 500.0,
            ),
            (
                at: 1040.0,
                kind: Orlan,
                path: [(1400.0, 5200.0), (600.0, 200.0), (-1200.0, -300.0), (-2200.0, -900.0), (-1800.0, 5200.0)],
            ),
            (
                at: 1250.0,
                kind: Zala,
                path: [(2900.0, -3200.0), (1500.0, -400.0), (300.0, 400.0), (2800.0, 1400.0)],
                agl: 500.0,
            ),
        ],
        interceptors: 3,
        radar: (at: (450.0, -60.0), range: 2000.0),
    ),
    // The day: about ten get in on a day like this (c15 §5), seeping from three sides at about 1.3 men an hour
    // (bav_sim::seep): the 51st CAA's from the south-eastern edge and the jaw, the 2nd CAA's from Pokrovsk's side onto
    // Rivne (c15 §4); the road through Svitle stays ours. Five robot runs by day, and the Vampire's two sorties at dusk; a KAB pair; the claim of
    // 1 December on the net (c15 §9), which changes nothing on the ground. The runs' times and cargoes are the
    // design's.
    script: [
        (2.0, Say("Bird up. Cloud, but it's dry. They can see everything today, and so can we.")),
        (
            30.0,
            Say(
                "All, this is {command}. Moscow says Pokrovsk is theirs. It changes nothing here. Nobody on the road by day.",
            ),
        ),
        // A robot makes 10 km/h, and the day's clock runs about eighteen times faster than the game's (c15 §5, the
        // Zmiy): a run of four kilometres is the day's clock from first light to dusk, so the long runs leave at
        // first light and are not back by dark. Food and water to the mine, where two wounded wait; fuel and batteries
        // for the drone team at the town's western entrance; ammunition to Svitle by the villages' tracks; and
        // ammunition, then food, to Rivne, the post nearest the road head, there and back. The robot left over goes
        // for the high-rise's wounded at first light (`robots.fetch`).
        (20.0, Ugv(to: 5, cargo: Food)),
        (60.0, Ugv(to: 6, cargo: Power)),
        (120.0, Ugv(to: 0, cargo: Ammo)),
        (180.0, Ugv(to: 1, cargo: Ammo)),
        (900.0, Ugv(to: 1, cargo: Food)),
        (
            150.0,
            Seep(
                route: 0,
                from: 450.0,
                width: 300.0,
                per_hour: 0.55,
                crews: 0.6,
                label: "08:45  Twos and threes at the south-eastern edge",
            ),
        ),
        (150.0, Seep(route: 1, from: 700.0, width: 300.0, per_hour: 0.45, crews: 0.4)),
        (150.0, Seep(route: 2, from: 1550.0, width: 300.0, per_hour: 0.3, crews: 0.15)),
        (
            600.0,
            Bombs(
                from: (300.0, 100.0),
                to: (500.0, 250.0),
                n: 2,
                label: "11:05  KABs on the western quarters",
                say: "Su-34s. Glide bombs. Down.",
            ),
        ),
        (1250.0, Say("This is {op}. It's getting dark. The road will be busy tonight.")),
        // As the light goes the Vampire, one sortie at a time: a bundle of ammunition for the high-rise (13:53), then
        // 60 mm bombs on the ruins by the mine, where the groups from the jaw go to ground (14:51).
        (1150.0, Sortie(to: (880.0, 525.0), load: Bundle(Ammo))),
        (1340.0, Sortie(to: (1600.0, -350.0), load: Bombs)),
    ],
)
